  "body": "I sent a link to the streams spec to a non-technical colleague and he was all like: \"this is too technical, I can't work out what it does\". \n\nCan we add a really simple list of funky examples of the kinds of things you can do with the API somewhere. It will help less technical people without experience in streams see new opportunities for the things that could be built using this.  \n\nLike: \n- Video effects: pipe a video stream into a custom video effects library. Apply the effects in real time. \n- Real time image analysis:  you could pipe a video into a module that scans for things like barcodes, people's faces, etc.\n- Real time transformations: you can convert one file format to another as the file is being downloaded. \n\nWe don't need to go crazy with the list... but just a few nice examples would better help communicate the intent of the spec to a wider audience. \n",
